<title>CANADA: CBRS reaffirms Gulf after Clyde deal.</title>
<headline>CBRS reaffirms Gulf after Clyde deal.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Bond Rating Service said on Tuesday that it has reaffirmed the ratings of Gulf Canada Resources Ltd following its acquisition of Clyde Petroleum Plc.</p>
<p>The debt rating agency reaffirmed Gulf Canada's senior debentures at B+ (high), senior subordinated debentures at B+ (low), preferred shares at P-4, and commercial paper at A-2 (low).</p>
<p>All ratings carry a positive outlook, CBRS said in a statement.  </p>
<p>&quot;The successful acquisition of Clyde provides Gulf with the international expansion that it had been seeking with established reserves and production in the North Sea, Australia, with additional assets in Indonesia,&quot; CBRS said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
